// SOUNDNESS QUEUE row arrayref_to_arrayptr_coercion_refused (tier 3).
// Legal Rust: `&[T; N]` coerces to `*const [T; N]` like any `&T -> *const T`.
// TODAY refused: "return type mismatch — expected *const [&'a i64; 3], got &'a [&'a i64; 3]"
// and "let 'p'/'q': type mismatch — expected *const [i64; 3], got &[i64; 3]". types_compatible's
// array-DECAY branch (`&[T; N]` -> `*const T`) answers first for every Array pointee and returns
// `types_compatible(elem, to.pointee())` — false for a `[T; N]` pointee — so the general
// `&T -> *const T` branch below it is never reached. Found 2026-09-14a-ptrcoerce (I11, K01, K02).
